  "question": {
    "text": "In Franck-Hertz experiment, the first dip in the current-voltage graph for hydrogen is observed at 10.2 V. The wavelength of light emitted by hydrogen atom when excited to the first excitation level is _________ $\\mathrm{nm}$. (Given $\\mathrm{hc}=1245 \\mathrm{eV} \\mathrm{nm}, \\mathrm{e}=1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\mathrm{C}$ ).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "122",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 10.2 \\mathrm{eV}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda} \\\\ & \\lambda=\\frac{1245 \\mathrm{eV}-\\mathrm{nm}}{10.2 \\mathrm{eV}}=122.06 \\mathrm{~nm}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
